// Analyzed file list for verilog_ethernet_fcs_roundtrip. Paths are relative to
// the PACKAGE ROOT: the elaboration recipe is sourced with the package root as
// cwd and `slang` is run from there too, so one spelling serves both.
//
// The round appends one `../submission/<worker>.sv` line per worker to the end
// of this file (v5/round.py), which resolves to <run_root>/submission from the
// same cwd. Do not add a trailing `-y`/library directive after the file list --
// an appended source line has to stay a source line.
//
// ONE analyzed file. The three verilog-ethernet RTL files are NOT listed:
// `ft/tb.sv` pulls them in with `include at file scope, exactly as the upstream
// task's `tcl/setup.tcl` does, and listing them as well would declare every
// module twice. `+incdir+rtl` is what makes those includes resolve.
+incdir+rtl

// --- the insert/check pair, the reference ring, the target and the covers ---
ft/tb.sv

// --- phase-1 candidate targets, LAST: a `bind` must be analyzed after the
// --- module it binds into --------------------------------------------------
sva/targets_verilog_ethernet_fcs_roundtrip.sv
